        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.station.fabricator.subtitle", "Manufacture implants, chipware, modules and workshop components in a 5x5 assembly grid.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.station.fabricator.operation", "Choose a learned or public design, inspect its layout, then use Fill grid and Fabricate. Fabrication repeats until ingredients run short or the output is full. Ingredients are consumed when each assembly completes. Stop leaves unfinished ingredients intact; Clear grid returns them. For automation, select a design, feed matching ingredients from above or the sides, and collect output from below. Each rising redstone edge starts exactly one craft. The signal may turn off while it runs. Pulses while busy or unable to craft are ignored, never queued; a held signal does not repeat. Configured schematic authorization survives reloads and does not require the player to stay online.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.station.fabricator.output", "A full output bay pauses assembly. No fuel, redstone power or external energy supply is required.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.station.fabricator.tiers", "Every Fabricator supports tiers 1-5 by default. Recipes still require their materials and any associated schematic.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.station.fabricator.schematics", "Right-click a schematic to learn it, consuming one item and gaining 10 XP points on first discovery. Already-learned schematics are not consumed. In the Neural Archive, you can pay to extract a learned design back into a schematic item. Relearning it gives no additional XP. Unknown designs appear in the Fabricator as black silhouettes with encrypted names, and remain uncraftable until learned. Their recipe details stay hidden from JEI and wiki layouts. Use the pin icon to keep a design at the top of the list.");
        add("screen.cyberneticenhancements.archive.schematic.extract", "Extract • %s €$");
        add("screen.cyberneticenhancements.archive.schematic.confirm_extract", "Confirm • %s €$");
        add("screen.cyberneticenhancements.archive.schematic.extract_tooltip", "Unlearn this design and recover the schematic item. Requires a free inventory slot.");
        add("message.cyberneticenhancements.schematic_extract.inventory_full", "Free an inventory slot to extract this schematic.");
        add("message.cyberneticenhancements.schematic_extract.insufficient", "Schematic extraction costs %s €$. Insufficient funds.");
        add("message.cyberneticenhancements.schematic_extract.success", "Extracted %s for %s €$.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.station.fabricator.collection", "The Schematics tab shows owned and missing designs. Missing designs use black silhouettes and encrypted names; their details cannot be opened. Learned designs show recipes and the original discovery history.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.station.upgrade.subtitle", "Improve the same physical implant through its server-defined +1 track.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.station.upgrade.overview", "Insert an uninstalled implant, supply up to two materials, and press Upgrade. A four-second cycle adds exactly one level to that same implant in place. Stop cancels unfinished work without consuming inputs. Hover the implant to inspect the next upgrade benefits. In Creative, Fill materials supplies the requirements for free. Inventory and progress stay in the station when closed. Hoppers and pipes insert implants and materials from above or the sides and retrieve the implant from below after an upgrade completes. Each rising redstone edge starts one upgrade; busy or invalid pulses are ignored and never queued.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.station.upgrade.condition", "Upgrading preserves current integrity, name, installed chips, modules and other item data. It never grants a repair.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.station.upgrade.cost", "Each step uses its server datapack price and adds exactly one level. The item page shows the current track, level cap and numerical benefits.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.station.upgrade.models", "The Upgrade Station never changes the model or manufactured tier. Model conversions use an explicit Fabricator recipe and its schematic requirements.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.station.upgrade.capacity", "Repair, Upgrade and Recycler stations support all implant tiers by default. No service capacity upgrades are required.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.service.separate_stations", "Repair restores integrity in 25% steps at a Repair Station. Upgrade +1 improves performance at an Upgrade Station without repairing wear.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.service.preserve_data", "Both operations keep the same implant, its name, upgrades and installed data. Fill materials transfers only the required amounts; an explicit action creates the completed item.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.service.no_schematic", "Routine repair and +1 upgrades require the implant and service materials, but no fabrication schematic.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.recycle.condition", "Recovery bands: at least %s%% integrity is good; %s%% to below that is worn; below %s%% is heavily damaged.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.recycle.example_good", "The illustrated batch is a full-integrity example. Insert your actual item into the Recycler to see its exact condition-dependent recovery.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.recycle.no_refund", "Each recycling cycle destroys one input and commits the entire previewed batch. Stored chips and modules are destroyed with their host; upgrades are not refunded and no schematic is learned.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.npc.stock_entry", "%sx %s — trust level %s");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.npc.shared_relationship", "Each contact keeps separate trust, services and meeting state for every player. Purchases use your eurodollar account.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.npc.role.fixer", "A broker for stabilization, selected cyberware stock and relic-cache route intel.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.npc.role.ripperdoc", "A medical contact providing suppression, healing and clinic stock. Implant installation still happens at a Ripper Station.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.npc.role.techie", "A workshop contact supplying neural parts, component bundles, utility implants, work buffs and contracts. Higher-grade component bundles unlock with trust.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.npc.role.netrunner", "A specialist in neural stock, scouting services, cache intel and breach-oriented contracts.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.npc.role.merc", "A field contact offering combat preparation, starter hardware and combat-oriented contracts.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.npc.services.fixer", "Strain buffer reduces effective cyberstrain by 18 for two minutes. Neural reset clears psychosis and active neural doses, once per world day.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.npc.services.ripperdoc", "Clinic care restores 8 health and supplies 24 suppression for three minutes. Detox restores 4 health, removes harmful effects and clears neural pressure once per world day.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.npc.services.techie", "Mining calibration gives Haste II for five minutes. Hazard preparation gives Fire Resistance and Resistance I for five minutes.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.npc.services.netrunner", "Recon support gives Night Vision and Speed I for eight minutes. Stealth protocol gives Invisibility and Speed I for three minutes; armor and held items remain visible.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.npc.services.merc", "Field recovery gives Regeneration I for 15 seconds and Absorption I for three minutes. Combat preparation gives Strength I and Resistance I for three minutes.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.npc.secondary_service", "The secondary service unlocks at trust level %s. Its current price and availability appear in the contact screen.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.npc.currency", "Payments withdraw eurodollars, not emeralds. Shops show the item's quantity, trust gate and current price before purchase.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.npc.discounts", "Trust can reduce this contact's prices, up to 25%% at maximum trust. Purchases, services and financial help share a daily commerce-trust budget per contact; the bundled limit is four trust points per Minecraft day. Completed contracts earn trust separately. Temporary heat can raise prices or cause refusal.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.npc.fixed_prices", "This archetype does not apply trust discounts. Trust still unlocks stock, services and identity options.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.npc.contracts_available", "This contact can issue contracts. The current board and active job appear in dialogue and the Quests tab.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.npc.no_contracts", "This archetype does not issue contracts. Visit a Techie, Netrunner or Merc for a job board.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.npc.intel_available", "Ask this contact about nearby relic caches. If a known cache remains unclaimed by you in this dimension, its location is marked on your HUD compass. Leads only cover caches already discovered by the server.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.npc.no_intel", "This archetype does not offer the cache-intel service.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.npc.identity_unlock", "Maximum trust unlocks the contact's identity customization options.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.controls.title", "Controls & Archive");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.controls.subtitle", "Your current key bindings and the archive's live tools.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.controls.binding", "%s: %s");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.controls.archive", "The Neural Archive contains the wiki, schematic collection, Tarot collection, banking, contacts, compass, quests and journal.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.banking.title", "Eurodollars & Banking");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.banking.subtitle", "Server-owned account funds for contact purchases and player payments.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.banking.operations", "Banking has Overview, Activity and Requests views. Overview shows your available balance, income, expenses and net change for the selected 7-, 14- or 30-day period. The money in/out graph separates daily income and spending. The balance history graph shows daily closing balances, with today showing your current balance. Both graphs share the selected period; hover a day for exact amounts. Daily totals are saved for 30 Minecraft days independently of the latest 120 individual transactions. Existing accounts start this history from their saved ledger. Use Activity to search and filter transactions, or Requests to pay, decline or cancel a request.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.banking.authority", "Transfers and purchases are validated by the server. A payment request does not withdraw money until the recipient accepts it.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.banking.sources", "Contracts credit your account when rewards are claimed. Contact purchases and paid services debit the same balance.");
